{"node":{"id":"HP:0002476","label":"Primitive reflex","ic":5.879,"definition":"The primitive reflexes are a group of behavioral motor responses which are found in normal early development, are subsequently inhibited, but may be released from inhibition by cerebral, usually frontal, damage. They are thus part of a broader group of reflexes which reflect release phenomena, such as exaggerated stretch reflexes and extensor plantars. They do however involve more complex motor responses than such simple stretch reflexes, and are often a normal feature in the neonate or infant."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0010099","label":"Tay-Sachs disease AB variant","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_f970ef38ef87","source":"MONDO:0010099","target":"HP:0002476","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:272750 · OMIM:272750","url":"https://omim.org/entry/272750","level":"curated","date":"2017-07-13","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"GM2-gangliosidosis, AB variant: Primitive reflex [TAS]"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:309246 · ORPHA:309246","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/309246","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"GM2 gangliosidosis, AB variant: Primitive reflex (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:309246","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/309246","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Primitive reflex — Frequent (79-30%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.6,"independent_sources":["OMIM","Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.6},{"id":"MONDO:0014147","label":"neuronal ceroid lipofuscinosis 13","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_6da20f8be025","source":"MONDO:0014147","target":"HP:0002476","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:615362 · OMIM:615362","url":"https://omim.org/entry/615362","level":"curated","date":"2015-12-30","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Ceroid lipofuscinosis,